course: dictionary
lesson: 10385
title: Shaking and trembling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tremble means to shake slightly, and not because you choose to. You might tremble because you are cold, afraid, excited or weak. «Toad trembles and holds on to the table leg.» Toad is holding on tightly, so his shaking is probably a sign that he is frightened or unsteady.
explain: Look at the words around the word to find out why something trembles. «The Mole panics, runs blindly, falls over things, and at last crawls into the hollow of an old beech tree, trembling.» He has just been panicking, so trembling shows he is shaking with fear.
explain: Trembling can also happen to a voice. «In a low, trembling voice» means the voice shakes a little, often because the speaker is nervous or upset. Nervousness can make the voice shake and the hands fidget or tremble. Ask yourself: why would this be shaking?
fact: Tremble can be a verb (to tremble) or a noun (a tremble).
fact: A tremble is a small shaking movement.
fact: Things can tremble too: leaves tremble in the wind, and the ground trembles in a small earthquake.
fact: Common phrases include «tremble with fear», «tremble with cold», «a trembling voice» and «hands trembling».
fact: A good check is to swap in the meaning, shake slightly, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Toad trembles and holds on to the table leg.» What does trembles mean here? | Sits down quietly | Laughs loudly | *Shakes slightly, without meaning to | Walks away fast
exercise: Ella felt a tremble in her hands before the test. What is a tremble? | A bright colour | A loud shout | *A small shaking movement | A long, deep sleep
exercise: «Nervousness can make the voice shake and the hands fidget or tremble.» What can make a voice tremble? | A new pair of shoes | *Nerves | Sleeping | Sunshine
test: Jo says, «My hands are trembling because it is freezing.» Why are Jo's hands trembling? | *Because she is cold | Because she is singing loudly | Because she is asleep | Because she is painting a picture
test: A leaf trembles in the wind. What is happening to the leaf? | It grows very big overnight | It falls off the tree forever | It turns into a bird | *It shakes slightly
exam: Which sentence uses tremble as a noun? | They tremble with fear | Toad trembles by the table | The leaves tremble in the wind | *He felt a tremble run through his legs
